                                "sense_id": "392ac47e-7a3f-3260-957b-b850a0a32bf7",
                                "text": "When I first met Damon, his nursery days of tadpolism were long ago past. He was out in the world, his own master, and pretended to forget that he was ever a tadpole, with enormous head and belly and a long tail."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d585b8ff-dfbf-46fc-be10-c9a8f00bde48",
                                "sense_id": "392ac47e-7a3f-3260-957b-b850a0a32bf7",
                                "text": "With such a source of wealth in one's pocket one would begin to live; all previous existence would be tadpolism, now only would one stretch out legs and arms and begin to jump."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
